	<item>
		<title>Terms and Conditions</title>
		<link>https://queendorfashionhouse.com/terms/</link>
		<pubDate>Sun, 02 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[queendor]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://queendorfashionhouse.com/?page_id=9101</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Last updated: [DATE]</strong></p>
<h3>1. Who we are</h3>
<p>This website, <strong>queendorfashionhouse.com</strong>, is operated by <strong>[REGISTERED BUSINESS
NAME]</strong>, a business registered in Ghana under registration number
<strong>[REGISTRATION NUMBER]</strong>, with its address at <strong>[BUSINESS ADDRESS, ACCRA,
GHANA]</strong>.</p>
<p>You can reach us by email at <strong>[EMAIL ADDRESS]</strong> or by telephone on <strong>[PHONE
NUMBER]</strong>. These are the same details that appear on our Contact page and in the
footer of every page of this site.</p>
<h3>2. What we sell</h3>
<p>We design, make and sell <strong>Adinkra-inspired jewellery</strong> — necklaces, earrings,
bracelets, rings and gift sets — hand-finished in Accra, Ghana. Pieces are sold
both to individual customers and, under separate wholesale terms, to retailers
and stockists.</p>
<p>Products are sold as described on each product page. Our jewellery is
<strong>hand-finished</strong>, so small variations in finish, tone and dimension between
pieces are normal and are not defects.</p>
<h3>3. Prices</h3>
<p>All prices are shown in <strong>Ghana cedis (GH₵)</strong> and are the price you pay for the
item. <strong>[Delete whichever does not apply: "Prices include VAT where applicable."
/ "We are not currently VAT-registered; no VAT is charged."]</strong></p>
<p>Delivery charges, where they apply, are shown separately before you pay. We may
change prices at any time, but a change never affects an order we have already
confirmed.</p>
<h3>4. Placing an order</h3>
<p>An order you place is an offer to buy. A contract is formed when we send you an
<strong>order confirmation email</strong>. If we cannot fulfil an order — a piece is out of
stock, the price was listed in error, or we cannot deliver to your address — we
will tell you and refund you in full.</p>
<p>We may refuse or cancel an order where we reasonably suspect fraud, where the
order is for resale outside our wholesale terms, or where the law requires it.</p>
<h3>5. Payment</h3>
<p>Payment is processed by <strong>Paystack</strong>, a payment service provider licensed by the
Bank of Ghana. You can pay by <strong>card (Visa, Mastercard)</strong> or <strong>mobile money (MTN
MoMo, Telecel Cash, AirtelTigo Money)</strong>.</p>
<p>We never see and never store your card number, expiry date, CVV or mobile money
PIN. Those details are entered on Paystack's secure checkout and handled by
Paystack alone, subject to their own terms and privacy policy.</p>
<p>Your order is only dispatched once payment has been confirmed by Paystack.</p>
<h3>6. Delivery</h3>
<p>We deliver within Ghana. Delivery times, charges and the areas we cover are set
out on our <strong>Delivery page</strong> (<code>/shipping-delivery/</code>), which forms part of these
terms.</p>
<p>Delivery times are estimates, not guarantees. Risk in the goods passes to you on
delivery. If a parcel is lost or damaged in transit, contact us and we will deal
with the courier on your behalf.</p>
<p>We do not currently ship outside Ghana.</p>
<h3>7. Returns, exchanges and refunds</h3>
<p>Our <strong>Returns and Refunds page</strong> (<code>/returns-exchanges/</code>) sets out your rights and
our policy in full, and forms part of these terms. In summary:</p>
<ul>
<li>Contact us within <strong>7 days</strong> of delivery to arrange a return or exchange.</li>
<li>The piece must be unworn, unaltered and in its original packaging.</li>
<li><strong>Earrings cannot be returned</strong> for hygiene reasons, unless they arrive damaged
  or faulty.</li>
<li><strong>Made-to-order and personalised pieces cannot be returned</strong> unless faulty.</li>
<li>If an item arrives damaged or we sent the wrong piece, we pay for the return and
  replace or refund it.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Refunds</strong> are made to the <strong>original payment method</strong> through Paystack, within
<strong>[NUMBER] working days</strong> of the returned item reaching us or of the refund being
agreed, whichever is later. We will confirm by email when a refund has been
issued. Bank and mobile money processing times are outside our control.</p>
<p>Nothing in this section affects any right you have under Ghanaian consumer law.</p>
<h3>8. Wholesale</h3>
<p>Wholesale pricing, minimum order quantities and account approval are governed by
our <strong>Wholesale page</strong> (<code>/wholesale/</code>) and by the separate agreement we send to
approved trade customers. Wholesale orders are not consumer sales.</p>
<h3>9. Care of your jewellery</h3>
<p>Guidance on looking after gold-plated, brass, silver and beaded pieces is on our
<strong>Care page / product pages</strong>. Damage caused by contact with perfume, lotion,
water, chlorine or abrasive cleaning is not a manufacturing fault.</p>
<p>If you have a known metal allergy, contact us before ordering and we will tell you
exactly what a piece is made of.</p>
<h3>10. Your information</h3>
<p>We collect and use your personal data in accordance with the <strong>Data Protection
Act, 2012 (Act 843)</strong>. Our <strong>Privacy Policy</strong> (<code>/privacy-policy/</code>) explains what we
collect, why, who we share it with and how long we keep it, and forms part of
these terms.</p>
<h3>11. Our content</h3>
<p>The photographs, designs, text and symbol artwork on this site belong to us. The
Adinkra symbols themselves are part of Ghanaian cultural heritage and belong to
everyone; our photographs and the pieces we make from them are ours. Please do not
reuse our images for commercial purposes without permission.</p>
<h3>12. Our responsibility to you</h3>
<p>We are responsible for loss you suffer that is a foreseeable result of our
breaking these terms or failing to use reasonable care. We are not responsible for
loss that was not foreseeable, for business losses where you are buying as a
consumer, or for events outside our reasonable control.</p>
<p>Nothing in these terms limits our liability for death or personal injury caused by
our negligence, for fraud, or for anything else that cannot lawfully be limited.
Where we are liable, our liability for any order is limited to <strong>the amount you
paid for that order</strong>.</p>
<h3>13. Complaints</h3>
<p>If something has gone wrong, contact us first at <strong>[EMAIL ADDRESS]</strong> or
<strong>[PHONE NUMBER]</strong> and give us the chance to put it right. We aim to respond within
<strong>two working days</strong>. If we cannot resolve it between us, Ghanaian law applies and
the courts of Ghana have jurisdiction.</p>
<h3>14. Changes to these terms</h3>
<p>We may update these terms from time to time. The version that applies to your
order is the version published when you placed it. The date at the top of this
page shows when it last changed.</p>
<hr />]]></content:encoded>
		<excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[]]></excerpt:encoded>
