	</item>
	<item>
		<title>About Us</title>
		<link>https://queendorfashionhouse.com/about/</link>
		<pubDate>Sun, 02 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[queendor]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://queendorfashionhouse.com/?page_id=9106</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Queen Dor's Fashion House</strong> makes <strong>Adinkra jewellery</strong> in Accra, Ghana. Gold-plated,
brass, sterling silver and beaded pieces — necklaces, earrings, bracelets, rings and
gift sets — sold <strong>retail to individual customers</strong> across Ghana and <strong>wholesale to
boutiques and stockists</strong>.</p>
<h3>The business</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th></th>
<th></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Registered name</strong></td>
<td><strong>[REGISTERED BUSINESS NAME]</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Trading as</strong></td>
<td>Queen Dor's Fashion House</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Registration number</strong></td>
<td><strong>[NUMBER]</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Business address</strong></td>
<td><strong>[STREET ADDRESS], [AREA], Accra, Ghana</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Email</strong></td>
<td><strong>[EMAIL ADDRESS]</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Phone</strong></td>
<td><strong>[PHONE NUMBER]</strong></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>What we make</h3>
<p>Every piece is built around an <strong>Adinkra symbol</strong>, and every symbol already means
something before we touch it.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Gye Nyame</strong> — the supremacy of the divine; what holds everything together.</li>
<li><strong>Sankofa</strong> — go back and fetch it; what you carry with you.</li>
<li><strong>Akoma</strong> — the heart; patience and endurance.</li>
<li><strong>Duafe</strong> — the wooden comb; care, and the beauty of good grooming.</li>
<li><strong>Dwennimmen</strong> — the ram's horns; humility alongside strength.</li>
<li><strong>Nkyinkyim</strong> — the twisting; adaptability, changing with circumstance.</li>
<li><strong>Adinkrahene</strong> — the chief of symbols; leadership and greatness.</li>
<li><strong>Bese Saka</strong> — the sack of cola nuts; wealth through unity.</li>
</ul>
<p>We did not invent these meanings and we do not need to. We make them wearable.</p>
<p><strong>Materials:</strong> gold-plated brass, solid brass, sterling silver, and hand-beaded
pieces. Each product page states what that piece is made of, its size and its
weight. Our jewellery is <strong>hand-finished in small batches</strong>, so small differences in
finish and dimension between pieces are normal and are not defects.</p>
<h3>How it is made</h3>
<p>Pieces are designed in Accra and hand-finished here, in small runs — cast or
assembled, filed, polished and plated before each one is boxed. Made-to-order pieces
are made after you order them, which is why they take longer and cannot be returned.</p>
<h3>Retail and wholesale</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Retail:</strong> order directly from this site. Prices are in Ghana cedis, and payment
  is by card or mobile money through <strong>Paystack</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>Wholesale:</strong> we supply boutiques and stockists. Minimum <strong>6 pieces per style</strong>,
  at <strong>50% of the retail price</strong>, boxed and retail-ready. Trade accounts are approved
  individually — see the <em>Wholesale</em> page.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Delivery and returns</h3>
<p>We deliver across Ghana: central Accra by dispatch rider in 1–2 working days, other
regions by courier in 2–4. Returns are accepted within 7 days, with the usual
exception of earrings for hygiene reasons. Full details are on the <em>Shipping &amp;
Delivery</em> and <em>Returns and Refunds</em> pages — those pages form part of our terms.</p>
<h3>Get in touch</h3>
<p><strong>[EMAIL ADDRESS]</strong> · <strong>[PHONE NUMBER]</strong> · [ADDRESS], Accra, Ghana
Instagram: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/queendor_fashionhouse/">@queendor_fashionhouse</a></p>
<p><em>Elegant jewellery for every occasion.</em></p>
<hr />]]></content:encoded>
